; slack_index_overflow: SLACK's appended indices are range-checked.
;
; capacity = 3 gives two slack bits, so SLACK appends start_index and
; start_index + 1. At start_index = i64::MAX the second one leaves the
; range. The program charges 64 bytes and passes at any default budget, so
; nothing else stops it: a bare `start_index + i` would panic in a build
; with overflow checks and wrap without them, or store 2^63 into the vec
; under unbounded integers. vector-ops/slack_append uses start_index 0 and
; does not reach this boundary.

VECI r0
VECI r1
PUSH 9223372036854775807   ; start_index
PUSH 3                     ; capacity
SLACK r0 r1
HALT
